  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an array AAA of size NNN.\n\nYou can do the following operation on the array:\n\n\nPick any 222 **distinct** indices iii and jjj such that Ai=AjA_i=A_jAi​=Aj​;\nChange all the elements between the indices iii and jjj to AiA_iAi​, i.e, for all kkk (i≤k≤j)(i \\leq k \\leq j)(i≤k≤j), set Ak=AiA_k=A_iAk​=Ai​.\nFind the **minimum** number of operations required to **sort** the array in non-decreasing order. If it is not possible to sort the array, print −1-1−1 instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN - the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ denoting the array AAA.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, the **minimum** number of operations required to **sort** the array. If it is not possible to sort the array, print −1-1−1 instead.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤N0 \\leq A_i \\leq N 0≤Ai​≤N",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n6\n1 2 1 3 4 3\n3\n3 1 2",
        "output": "2\n-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 111: We can sort the array using 222 operations.\n\nIn the first operation select indices 111 and 333. After this operation, the array will be A=[1,1,1,3,4,3]A = [1,1,1,3,4,3]A=[1,1,1,3,4,3].\nIn the second operation select indices 444 and 666. After this operation, the array will be A=[1,1,1,3,3,3]A = [1,1,1,3,3,3]A=[1,1,1,3,3,3].\n\nThus, the array is sorted using 222 operations. It can be proven that the array cannot be sorted in less than 222 operations.\nTest Case 222: It is not possible to sort the array using any number of operations."
      }
    ]
  },
